This challenge boasts that it is the first full kill-chain case in the learning path.

Its learning objectives are:
- Master basic KQL syntax, including where, take, and distinct commands
- Effectively filter data to focus on relevant information
- Apply time-based filters to investigate events surrounding suspicious indicators
- Correlate events to construct comprehensive attack timelines
- Interpret PowerShell scripts and malicious commands run by attackers

It is tagged with: data-exfiltration, phishing, and influence operations.


Section 1 is KQL101.
I have to determine how many employees work at this organization.
Employees
| count
Answer: 100

Find the Editorial Director's name. Lets try:
Employees
| where role == "Editorial Director"
Answer: Nene Leaks

How many emails did Nene receive? 
Emails
| where recipient == "nene_leaks@valdoriantimes.news"
| count
Answer: 18

How many distinct SENDERS were there from the domain weprinturstuff.com?
Emails
| where sender contains "weprinturstuff.com"
| distinct sender
| count
Answer: 100

How many distinct URLs did “Lois Lane” visit?
Employees
| where name == "Lois Lane"
And with this, I see that Lois's IP is 10.10.0.22. Next:
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip == "10.10.0.22"
| distinct url
| count 
Answer: 62

How many distinct domains in the PassiveDns records contain the word “hire”?
PassiveDns
| where domain contains "hire"
| distinct domain
| count
Answer: 6

What IPs did the domain “jobhire.org” resolve to (enter any one of them)?
PassiveDns
| where domain contains "jobhire.org"
| distinct ip
Answer: 191.7.248.112

How many distinct websites did employees with the first name "Mary" Visit?
let mary_ips = 
Employees
| where name has "Mary"
| distinct ip_addr;
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip in (mary_ips)
| count
